"features.md#xp-feature-nix-command) and its interface is subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix store submit-output` - submit a store object as one of the outputs of "
"the derivation currently being built"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:12
msgid "`nix store submit-output` \\[_option_...\\] _path_ _output_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:16
msgid ""
"To submit a given [store object](../../store/store-object.md) as the output "
"named `out`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:22
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:24
msgid ""
"`nix store submit-output` registers a [store object](../../store/store-"
"object.md) as an output of the currently-running derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-submit-output.md:26
msgid ""
"It only functions when running inside a content-addressing derivation with "
"the `builder-rpc-v0` system feature, which provides a limited daemon socket "
"to the builder. Execution in any other environment will fail."
msgstr ""

